## 2. `/dayjs/test/plugin/timezone.test.js` (175 lines)
- `describe('Parse')` is at line 27, containing `'parse target time string'` (28–37) and `'parse and convert between timezones'` (39–43). **The test `'Parse parse timestamp, js Date, Day.js object'` is not present anywhere in the repo** (confirmed by grep), consistent with the task statement. It belongs in `describe('Parse')`.
- Existing tests only ever pass **strings** to `dayjs.tz(...)` (e.g. lines 29, 40, 92, 103, …), so the bug is not exercised. Running `npx jest test/plugin/timezone.test.js --coverage=false` on the pristine repo: **14/14 pass**.

## 3. Core `/dayjs/src/index.js` parse/constructor
```js
